<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch bonds close at two-month peak.</title>
<headline>Dutch bonds close at two-month peak.</headline>
<text>
<p>---------------------(Snapshot at 1540 GMT)---------------------</p>
<p>*CASH YIELDS (Dutch state loans)</p>
<p> July 1998 6.25 pct   103.11/19 (+0.04)   bid yield 3.47 (-0.05)</p>
<p> Feb  2002		115.09/19 (+0.24)		 4.63 (-0.06)</p>
<p> Feb  2007 5.75 pct   101.22/32 (+0.42)		 5.58 (-0.06)</p>
<p> Jan  2023		114.71/91 (+0.80)		 6.32 (-0.06)</p>
<p>*FUTURES</p>
<p> BUNDS (June)	  102.24 (+0.47)</p>
<p> TREASURIES (June)   110.38 (+0.54 vs pvs Dutch close)</p>
<p>*DM/NLG		    1.1250 (PREV 1.1247)</p>
<p>--------------------------(SPREADS)----------------------------</p>
<p>*DSLs versus Bunds  (pvs close)    *DSL curve     (pvs close)</p>
<p> 5 yr	 -0.01	LEVEL	  10-2 yr  211     (212)</p>
<p> 10 yr	-0.08	-0.10	  10-5 yr   95	(95)</p>
<p> Long	 -0.15	-0.16</p>
<p>---------------------------(May 12)-----------------------------</p>
<p>* Dutch bonds end at two-month high as German bund futures surge up through 102.00 level.</p>
<p>* But gains achieved on barely-detectable turnover as institutions continue to shy away from guilder paper.</p>
<p>* Eyes ahead to U.S. and German data this week.</p>
